                                                        <p class="brfprofile">

                                                            <b>Brief Profile:</b>

                                                            Prof. Charul Sharma is an Assistant Professor at GNIOT Institute of Management Studies, Greater Noida, Delhi/NCR, and a two-time research paper presenter at the prestigious <b>IIM Conference</b>, showcasing her strong academic presence and dedication to impactful research.

<br>At GIMS, she currently heads the Alumni Relations, Internationalization, and Placement Audit departments, in addition to managing campus placements. She is presently pursuing her doctorate from Sharda University and is actively associated with the PhD House Chamber of Commerce & Industry. 

<br>Her research interests lie in the evolving role of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in Human Resource Management (HR), with a focus on how AI transforms employee engagement, recruitment practices, and organizational effectiveness. 

<br>Prof. Sharma has previously worked as a Research Associate at JIMS Rohini and Jaypee Institute. Her scholarly contributions include multiple publications indexed in ABDC, Scopus, and Web of Science, and she holds a registered Intellectual Property Right (IPR). 

<br>Academically, she holds an MBA from AKTU, a PGDM from IMT Ghaziabad, and a B.Sc. in Biotechnology from ITS College under CCSU. With over six years of teaching experience, she specializes in Human Resource Management (HRM) and Organizational Behavior (OB). 

<br>She has conducted tutorials for management students and has presented her work at numerous national and international conferences, also serving as a session chair at several academic forums. 

<br>Her professional certifications include Database Training, IBM Practitioners Badge for Design Thinking, Ludifu Student Partner (LSP) Program, Ludifu Workshop on Power BI, and a certification in Organic and Natural Farming from the National Centre for Organic and Natural Farming, Ghaziabad, where she also served as a master trainee and lecturer. 

<br>She is a certified educator of Human Values and Professional Ethics, having completed AICTE-approved Level-1 training, along with participation in an ethics-based project in collaboration with IISc Bangalore. 

<br>In the corporate sector, Prof. Sharma has worked with Newgen Software Technologies, Ananta Resource Management, and JBM Group, where she was recognized with the Best Recruiter Award for her exceptional contributions in talent acquisition and candidate engagement. 

<br>With a strong belief in lifelong learning and institutional advancement, Prof. Charul Sharma envisions contributing to academic innovation, student development, and industry-aligned education. She is deeply committed to supporting the continuous progress of GIMS as a premier institution in management education. 

                                                        </p>

